Subject: [overlay 0043] DRAWDIAG — the per-eye light question asked where pixels are decided

R19 item 2 is the other half of the base1 report: at one spot a wall is "LIGHT in my left
eye, DARK in my right eye". 0042's header shows the CLIENT cannot cause that — the light
selection reads cl.refdef.vieworg before view.c injects the per-eye pose, so both eyes select
the identical set (measured: LIGHTDIAG lh identical on 1841/1841 walk pairs). So the split, if
it exists, is in the refresh.

0040's LIGHTDIAG already prints `marked=` and `bh=` (a hash of every world face's dlightbits),
but it samples them immediately after GL_MarkLights — BEFORE the entity and alpha passes, both
of which write face stamps (world.c re-stamps an inline bmodel's alpha faces with the world's
stamp, 0039). That is why eye 1 legitimately reports 5-10 more marked faces than eye 0 for the
same host frame: eye 0's own bmodel pass stamped them after eye 0's sample was taken. The
instrument therefore cannot distinguish "the two eyes light faces differently" from "the two
eyes were measured at different points in the pipeline".

DRAWDIAG closes that. In GL_DrawFace — the single place a face's dlightbits reach a batch, and
the place 0039's stamp gate decides whether they count — this accumulates an ORDER-INDEPENDENT
hash over (face index, the bits that face actually contributed), plus the face count and the
number of faces whose bits the gate rejected. It is printed at the very END of R_RenderFrame,
after every pass. Two renders of the same host frame that drew the same faces with the same
lights produce identical faces/gated/dbh; any difference between eye 0 and eye 1 IS the per-eye
lighting divergence, at the last point before the shader.

Diagnostic only: everything is under the existing gl_lightdiag cvar (default 0), and the cost
when it is off is one already-loaded branch per batched face. No rendering behaviour changes.

Apply: patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this
--- a/src/refresh/gl.h
+++ b/src/refresh/gl.h
@@ -156,6 +156,17 @@
     // use (artifacts/vr-r14c/after/).
     unsigned        dlightframe_high;
     bool            repeat_frame;
+    // [vr overlay 0043] DRAW-TIME per-eye light instrument (diagnostic only). GL_DrawFace
+    // accumulates, for every face it batches, an order-independent hash of (face index, the
+    // dlightbits that face actually contributed after 0039's stamp gate). Two renders of the
+    // same host frame that drew the same faces with the same lights produce the same hash;
+    // a difference between eye 0 and eye 1 is a PER-EYE LIGHTING DIVERGENCE at the only place
+    // that decides pixels. LIGHTDIAG's marked/bh are sampled right after GL_MarkLights, which
+    // is before the entity and alpha passes have touched any stamps, so they cannot answer
+    // this question on their own.
+    uint32_t        drawlight_hash;
+    uint32_t        drawlight_gated;    // faces whose bits failed the stamp gate
+    int             drawlight_faces;
     int             viewcluster1;
     int             viewcluster2;
     int             nodes_visible;
--- a/src/refresh/tess.c
+++ b/src/refresh/tess.c
@@ -946,6 +946,19 @@
     // of lights per batch. Upstream bug, upstreamable as-is.
     if (surf->dlightframe == glr.dlightframe)
         tess.dlight_bits |= surf->dlightbits;
+
+    // [vr overlay 0043] the draw-time per-eye instrument (see gl.h). Costs one branch per
+    // face when gl_lightdiag is 0, which is every shipped frame.
+    if (gl_lightdiag->integer) {
+        uint64_t bits = (surf->dlightframe == glr.dlightframe) ? surf->dlightbits : 0;
+        uint32_t h = 2166136261u ^ (uint32_t)(surf - gl_static.world.cache->faces);
+        h = (h * 16777619u) ^ (uint32_t)(bits & 0xffffffffu);
+        h = (h * 16777619u) ^ (uint32_t)(bits >> 32);
+        glr.drawlight_hash += h;    // commutative: batch ORDER must not change the hash
+        glr.drawlight_faces++;
+        if (surf->dlightframe != glr.dlightframe && surf->dlightbits)
+            glr.drawlight_gated++;
+    }
 }
 
 void GL_ClearSolidFaces(void)
--- a/src/refresh/main.c
+++ b/src/refresh/main.c
@@ -944,6 +944,11 @@
 
     glr.fd = *fd;
     glr.ppl_bits  = 0;
+
+    // [vr overlay 0043] reset the draw-time light instrument for this render (see gl.h)
+    glr.drawlight_hash = 0;
+    glr.drawlight_faces = 0;
+    glr.drawlight_gated = 0;
 
     if (gl_dynamic->integer != 1 || gl_vertexlight->integer)
         glr.fd.num_dlights = 0;
@@ -1032,6 +1037,18 @@
 
     if (gl_showerrors->integer > 1)
         GL_ShowErrors(__func__);
+
+    // [vr overlay 0043] THE DRAW-TIME PER-EYE ANSWER. Printed after every pass that can touch
+    // a face's stamp or bits has run, unlike LIGHTDIAG which is sampled right after
+    // GL_MarkLights. dbh is an order-independent hash over (face, the bits that face actually
+    // contributed to its batch); faces is how many faces were batched; gated counts faces
+    // that carried bits the stamp gate rejected. eye 0 and eye 1 of the same host frame must
+    // agree on all three — a difference is a per-eye lighting divergence at the point where
+    // pixels are decided.
+    if (gl_lightdiag->integer)
+        Com_Printf("DRAWDIAG eye=%d rep=%d faces=%d gated=%u dbh=%08x\n",
+                   q2vr.active ? q2vr.eye : -1, glr.repeat_frame ? 1 : 0,
+                   glr.drawlight_faces, glr.drawlight_gated, glr.drawlight_hash);
 }
 
